637 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 301 0 R
/E (Based on Dealroom data for the period 2019 to 2024, CEE attracted EUR 4 billion out of EUR 44.68 billion in VC investment in transportation across the EU, representing less than 9%, despite the region generating 13% of EU GDP and 16% of transport value added. Excluding mega rounds, CEE attracted EUR 993 million out of EUR 19.27 billion across the EU, accounting for approximately 5.1% of the total.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
638 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 301 0 R
/E (The average level of investment in MobilityTech across the European Union is largely driven by a few of the largest and most mature ecosystems. Dealroom data for the period 2019 to 2024 shows that Germany accounts for approximately 26% of VC investment value in MobilityTech in the EU, Sweden for around 27%, and France for nearly 18%. This means that these three countries generate over 70% of all VC investment in the mobility sector in the EU.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
