730 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 307 0 R
/E (Poland is the EU leader in road freight transport, reaching 368 billion tonne kilometers in 2024, representing around 20% of total EU volume, compared to 281 billion in Germany and 272 billion in Spain. Despite this operational scale, none of the 15 European mobility unicorns originate from Poland, while Germany has 7, Sweden 3, France 2, and within CEE only Estonia is represented by Bolt.)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
731 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 307 0 R
/E (In the Polish technology ecosystem, there is a limited number of unicorn scale companies, among which InPost stands out as an example of a logistics company with international reach, originating from an early stage development model similar to a startup. InPost is typically classified as a mature public logistics company rather than a mobility startup, which is the main reason it is not included in the analyzed dataset.)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
