/P 315 0 R
/E (The EU aims to reduce emissions by 55% by 2030 and to ban the sale of new internal combustion engine cars from 2035. By 2050, more than 83% of EU residents will live in cities. In CEE countries such as Poland, the Czech Republic, and Hungary, wages have been growing at around 12% annually since 2022, increasing pressure for automation. However, this process may be slowed by regulatory uncertainty and uneven adoption rates across EU countries.)
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [3]
